ng  galadriel's brother as a corrupted  warlord borders on the sacrilegious at  the very least it'll be fascinating to  see how mckay and payne might attempt to  pull off a twist like this  prince duran iv is said to be one of the  most important dwarven characters in the  rings of power but who is he during the  fourth is a second age ruler of causa  doom and a bearer of one of the rings of  power his name is important every once  in a while a prince or king of the house  of durian is born who is almost  identical in appearance and manner to  during the deathless eldest of the  dwarves who first awoke many millennia  ago these dwarves are named durin and  are believed by their kin to be a  genuine reincarnation of the original in  total six dwarves have been given the  name during throughout middle earth's  history while it's currently unclear  what specific part prince during will  have to play in the series it will have  something to do with keller brimmwar's  forge and you can safely bet he'll be  playing it from within the kingdom of  kaza doom later known as morya tolkien  writes in the lord of the rings that  even as sauron's forces spread across  middle-earth khalsa doom remained  unconquered due to the strength and  bravery of its people prince durian will  likely lead them for much of the show's  run  the dwarven storyline in the rings of  power poses a curious question if during  the fourth is the prince of causa doom  who's the king the answer during the  third despite the fact that in tolkien's  writings during the third and during the  fourth live thousands of years apart  they'll be brought together as father  and son in the new series by its  condensed timeline this will avoid huge  time jumps and associated issues with  human characters mortality you've always  had sandstone in your granite as far as  the elves were concealed  in the original text during the third  has a much more explicit role in the  events surrounding sauron's rise than  during t