g  muriel daughter of tarpon tear the  previous king after sauron conquers much  of middle earth and declares himself  king of men uninfuriated farzone invades  the mainland swiftly and decisively  defeating the dark lord when the  numenoreans take sauron back to their  homeland as a hostage however he quickly  gets to work corrupting them for his own  ends far zone's subsequent fall into  darkness has world changing consequences  it appears that at the beginning of  season 1 farzone is merely a subject of  tar polynei and an advisor to his future  wife muriel the show's far zone is a  brilliant authoritative and  self-important type which suggests the  character's wicked personality is  already fully formed even if his tragic  fate has yet to play out  muriel is the daughter of tarpalantir  the king of numenor and the unwilling  wife to be of far zone tolkien wrote  little about tarmurial aside from the  disturbing nature of her marriage but it  appears that she'll be a significant  part of the numenorean storyline in the  rings of power it appears that muriel  will experience visions of numenor's  eventual destruction it's also reported  that muriel will be a queen during the  events of the show though her father is  still alive it's not yet known why this  might be it's said that she'll be a  savvy intelligent and compassionate  ruler and will see action in at least  one battle after joining the numenorean  expedition to middle-earth it's clear  that the show's version of muriel will  have much more impact on the history of  middle-earth than her literary  counterpart  tarpalantir is unusual among the late  kings of numenor though his immediate  predecessors mistrusted the elves and  the godlike valor he takes a royal name  in the elvish language quenya as well as  the  title tar as opposed to r taken from the  numenorean language this puts him at  odds with his own people who are  provoked by far zone into open rebellion  after tar polynei dies far zone usurps  